# Who is asked to review what. See GOVERNANCE.md.
#
# Each project profile has one slot for profile reviewers. There are two kinds
# (GOVERNANCE.md, Profile reviewers): a representative, who works on that
# project, and an external steward, who has no tie to it and looks after the
# profile when no representative is interested. The slot can hold either kind
# or both. Until a reviewer takes a slot, the line names the maintainers. Do not
# leave a line with no owner: GitHub then treats the file as having no code
# owner at all. To take a slot, open a pull request that adds your handle to the
# line, and add your affiliation and your kind to MAINTAINERS.md in the same
# pull request. An external steward is appointed by the maintainers first,
# through a public issue.
# Do not add a representative to a conflicted line below. Their fact check is
# welcome as a review comment, but it does not replace the required approval.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owners of a file when a pull request is
# ready for review (not while it is a draft). Branch protection decides whether
# that review is required. When it is required, an approval from any one owner
# on the line is enough. GitHub ignores an owner with no write access to this
# repository.

*                                    @mauromorales

# Conflicted files (GOVERNANCE.md, "Bootstrap"). The first maintainer with no
# affiliation to Kairos, Hadron Linux or Spectro Cloud replaces @mauromorales on
# these lines as the required approver. Adding them next to @mauromorales would
# not make their approval required, because any one owner on a line is enough.
# data/lineage.yaml, site/projects_meta.yaml, site/content.py and
# site/drafts/base_choice.yaml state facts about Kairos, Hadron and Spectro Cloud
# next to facts about the other projects. GitHub cannot protect one entry of a
# file, so the whole file is listed. Only a change that touches an entry about
# Kairos, Hadron or Spectro Cloud is conflicted. This file and MAINTAINERS.md
# are listed so that the hand-over cannot be undone by one approval. Any other
# file that states a fact about these projects counts the same way. For
# example site/build.py holds one such label, the fleet server name of Kairos.
# It is code, so it is not listed here, and the rule still applies to it.
# GOVERNANCE.md holds the ownership, administrator and removal rules. A change
# to it is conflicted, and for 24 months after the bootstrap ends the founder
# clause in it also needs the owner's agreement.
